# Cisco Umbrella API credentials, from the Umbrella admin console:
# Admin > API Keys (or Console Settings > API Keys on a Multi-org/MSP
# console). The API Secret is shown only once at creation time and cannot
# be retrieved later - store it somewhere safe immediately.
# Used by stdio and by HTTP when AUTH_MODE=env. The gateway Compose service
# does not load these. Do not add them to that service's environment or via
# env_file.
CISCOUMBRELLA_API_KEY=
CISCOUMBRELLA_API_SECRET=

# stdio (default) or http
# MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio

# Required to start the HTTP transport. Leave this empty here.
# The process logs an error and exits non-zero when this is empty or a known
# placeholder (replace-with-a-real-secret, your-s2s-secret, changeme, secret,
# example, ...), so a copied example cannot forge X-Gateway-S2S. Compose will
# not start when it is unset or empty. Never commit a real value.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
CONDUIT_S2S_SECRET=

# Local development only. Set to exactly 1 to start HTTP without
# CONDUIT_S2S_SECRET. Logs a warning, does not enforce X-Gateway-S2S, and
# binds 127.0.0.1 only. A non-loopback MCP_HTTP_HOST refuses to start.
# A known placeholder secret is still refused. Do not use in production.
# MCP_ALLOW_INSECURE_DEV=1

# Bind address for HTTP. When MCP_HTTP_HOST is unset, the server binds
# 127.0.0.1. A configured CONDUIT_S2S_SECRET honors this value. The container
# image sets 0.0.0.0.
# MCP_HTTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
# MCP_HTTP_PORT=8080

# gateway (Docker image and Compose default) or env.
# Gateway mode requires X-CiscoUmbrella-Api-Key and X-CiscoUmbrella-Api-Secret
# on each /mcp request and never falls back to CISCOUMBRELLA_*.
# AUTH_MODE=gateway

# LOG_LEVEL=info
